  <paragraph>The expressions in the next example have several factors in common. Remember to write the GCF as the product of all the common factors.</paragraph>
  <example number="7.7">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor: $$12x - 60$$ .</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Find the GCF of 12x and 60.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Rewrite each term as a product using the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check by mulitplying the factors.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$12(x - 5)$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$12 \cdot x - 12 \cdot 5$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$12x - 60✓$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
