  <paragraph>When the leading coefficient is negative, we factor the negative out as part of the GCF.</paragraph>
  <example number="7.12">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor: $$-8y - 24$$ .</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <paragraph>When the leading coefficient is negative, the GCF will be negative.</paragraph>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Ignoring the signs of the terms, we first find the GCF of 8y and 24 is 8. Since the expression −8y − 24 has a negative leading coefficient, we use −8 as the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Rewrite each term using the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$-8(y + 3)$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$-8 \cdot y + (-8) \cdot 3$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>$$-8y - 24✓$$</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
